<section class="bloc-texte" id="confidentialite">
    <h2>Privacy</h2>
    <p><strong>Visit counting.</strong> To know how many people visit the site, each page view is recorded in our own database, hosted on our own server,
    with no third-party analytics service or external script. We record only: the date, the page viewed, the country (deduced from your IP address with a file stored on our own server, without calling any external service),
    whether the visitor is a robot, and a fingerprint of your IP address.</p>
    <p><strong>Your IP address is never stored.</strong> It is turned into a one-way code, calculated with a secret key known only to our server: this code lets us count the same person only once,
    but the address cannot be recovered from it. This code changes at the start of each month: it cannot be used to follow you beyond a month. Visits are automatically deleted after 400 days.
    If your browser sends the “Do Not Track” (DNT) or “Global Privacy Control” (GPC) signal, your visit is not counted.</p>
    <p><strong>Cookies and storage.</strong> No advertising or audience-measurement cookies, no third-party trackers. Your choice of name display
    (“First Last” / “Last First”) is remembered only in your browser (local storage); it is never sent to the server.
    One functional cookie remembers your choice of language (and, once several countries are published, of country) for one year: it holds no personal data and is never used to track you.
    A login cookie exists only for the site's administration.</p>
    <p>Like any server, this one may note operating errors in its technical logs, for operation and security. Links to official sites take you away from this site: their own rules then apply.</p>
    <p><strong>Your rights.</strong> For any question or request about your data (access, deletion), write to <a href="mailto:contact@rebisway.com">contact@rebisway.com</a>.
    As we keep no accounts or user lists, we generally hold no data about you beyond this anonymised counting.</p>
</section>
}
